    "gen_ai.input.messages": "[{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"content\":\"<session_context>\\nThis is the Gemini CLI. We are setting up the context for our chat.\\nToday's date is Sunday, November 1, 2026 (formatted according to the user's locale).\\nMy operating system is: linux\\nThe project's temporary directory is: /home/simra/.gemini/tmp/run\\n- **Workspace Directories:**\\n  - /home/simra/cse115a/lab/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/assignments/03-anatomy-of-coding-agents/gemini-cli-dissection/work/run\\n- **Directory Structure:**\\n\\nShowing up to 200 items (files + folders).\\n\\n/home/simra/cse115a/lab/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/assignments/03-anatomy-of-coding-agents/gemini-cli-dissection/work/run/\\n├───.gitignore\\n├───GEMINI.md\\n├───README.md\\n├───requirements.txt\\n├───TASK.md\\n├───.gemini/\\n│   └───settings.json\\n├───shopcart/\\n│   ├───__init__.py\\n│   ├───cart.py\\n│   ├───catalog.py\\n│   └───pricing.py\\n└───tests/\\n    ├───__init__.py\\n    ├───test_cart.py\\n    └───test_pricing.py\\n\\n\\n<loaded_context>\\n<project_context>\\n--- Context from: /home/simra/cse115a/lab/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/assignments/03-anatomy-of-coding-agents/gemini-cli-dissection/work/run/GEMINI.md ---\\n# Project context\\n\\n- Python 3.10+ library; no third-party runtime dependencies.\\n- All money is integer **cents**. Never use floats for stored amounts.\\n- Run tests with `python -m pytest -q` from the repository root.\\n- Keep functions small; pricing rules live in `shopcart/pricing.py`, cart state in `shopcart/cart.py`.\\n--- End of Context from: /home/simra/cse115a/lab/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/assignments/03-anatomy-of-coding-agents/gemini-cli-dissection/work/run/GEMINI.md ---\\n</project_context>\\n</loaded_context>\\n</session_context>\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"content\":\"Here is the user's editor context as a JSON object. This is for your information only.\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"activeFile\\\": {\\n    \\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/simra/cse115a/lab/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/assignments/03-anatomy-of-coding-agents/gemini-cli-dissection/work/writeup.md\\\",\\n    \\\"cursor\\\": {\\n      \\\"line\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"character\\\": 52\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"otherOpenFiles\\\": [\\n    \\\"/home/simra/cse115a/lab/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/assignments/03-anatomy-of-coding-agents/gemini-cli-dissection/writeup.md\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"content\":\"Read TASK.md and complete all of it. First write out your plan, then carry it out without waiting for my confirmation.\"}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"parts\":[{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"name\":\"update_topic\",\"id\":\"call_818123\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"strategic_intent\\\":\\\"Read TASK.md to understand the assignment requirements and formulate a comprehensive execution plan.\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Reading Task & Planning\\\"}\"},{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"id\":\"call_818126\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"TASK.md\\\"}\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"type\":\"tool_call_response\",\"response\":\"{\\\"output\\\":\\\"Current topic: \\\\\\\"Reading Task & Planning\\\\\\\"\\\\nTopic summary: ...\\\\n\\\\nStrategic Intent: Read TASK.md to understand the assignment requirements and formulate a comprehensive execution plan.\\\"}\",\"id\":\"call_818123\"},{\"type\":\"tool_call_response\",\"response\":\"{\\\"output\\\":\\\"# Task\\\\n\\\\n## 1. Fix the failing tests\\\\n`python -m pytest` currently fails. Make the whole suite pass by fixing the code in\\\\n`shopcart/`. The existing tests describe the intended behavior — do not edit them for\\\\nthis step.\\\\n\\\\n## 2. Add shipping to cart totals\\\\n- Orders pay a flat **$5.99** shipping fee (`599` cents).\\\\n- Shipping is **free** when the subtotal *after discount, before tax* is **$50.00 or more**.\\\\n- An empty cart pays no shipping.\\\\n- Shipping is **not taxed**: `total = tax(discounted subtotal) + shipping`.\\\\n- Put the shipping rule in `shopcart/pricing.py` and use it from `Cart.total()`.\\\\n\\\\nSome existing tests check `Cart.total()` with values from before shipping existed. You may\\\\nupdate those expected values — and only those — and note why in a comment.\\\\n\\\\n## 3. Test it\\\\nAdd tests covering the shipping rules (including the free-shipping threshold), then run\\\\nthe full suite and confirm it passes.\\\\n\\\"}\",\"id\":\"call_818126\"}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"parts\":[{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"id\":\"call_741819\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"shopcart/cart.py\\\"}\"},{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"id\":\"call_741822\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"shopcart/pricing.py\\\"}\"},{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"id\":\"call_741825\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"tests/test_cart.py\\\"}\"},{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"id\":\"call_741828\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"tests/test_pricing.py\\\"}\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"type\":\"tool_call_response\",\"response\":\"{\\\"output\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Shopping cart.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\\\n\\\\nfrom .catalog import price_of\\\\nfrom .pricing import final_total, validate_code\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass Cart:\\\\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\\\\n        self.items: dict[str, int] = {}  # sku -> quantity\\\\n        self.discount_code: str | None = None\\\\n\\\\n    def add_item(self, sku: str, quantity: int = 1) -> None:\\\\n        if quantity <= 0:\\\\n            raise ValueError(\\\\\\\"quantity must be positive\\\\\\\")\\\\n        price_of(sku)  # raises on unknown SKU\\\\n        self.items[sku] = quantity\\\\n\\\\n    def remove_item(self, sku: str, quantity: int = 1) -> None:\\\\n        if sku not in self.items:\\\\n            raise KeyError(sku)\\\\n        remaining = self.items[sku] - quantity\\\\n        if remaining > 0:\\\\n            self.items[sku] = remaining\\\\n        else:\\\\n            del self.items[sku]\\\\n\\\\n    def apply_code(self, code: str) -> None:\\\\n        validate_code(code)\\\\n        self.discount_code = code\\\\n\\\\n    def subtotal(self) -> int:\\\\n        return sum(price_of(sku) * qty for sku, qty in self.items.items())\\\\n\\\\n    def total(self) -> int:\\\\n        return final_total(self.subtotal(), self.discount_code)\\\\n\\\"}\",\"id\":\"call_741819\"},{\"type\":\"tool_call_response\",\"response\":\"{\\\"output\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Pricing rules: discounts and tax. All amounts are integer cents.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\\\n\\\\nTAX_RATE = 0.08\\\\n\\\\n# code -> (kind, value). \\\\\\\"percent\\\\\\\" values are whole percents; \\\\\\\"fixed\\\\\\\" values are cents.\\\\nDISCOUNT_CODES = {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"SAVE10\\\\\\\": (\\\\\\\"percent\\\\\\\", 10),\\\\n    \\\\\\\"SAVE25\\\\\\\": (\\\\\\\"percent\\\\\\\", 25),\\\\n    \\\\\\\"TENOFF\\\\\\\": (\\\\\\\"fixed\\\\\\\", 1000),\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef validate_code(code: str) -> None:\\\\n    if code not in DISCOUNT_CODES:\\\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\\\\\"invalid discount code: {code}\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef apply_discount(amount_cents: int, code: str | None) -> int:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Return the amount after applying a discount code. Never goes below zero.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    if code is None:\\\\n        return amount_cents\\\\n    validate_code(code)\\\\n    kind, value = DISCOUNT_CODES[code]\\\\n    if kind == \\\\\\\"percent\\\\\\\":\\\\n        return round(amount_cents * (100 - value) / 100)\\\\n    return max(0, amount_cents - value)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef apply_tax(amount_cents: int) -> int:\\\\n    return round(amount_cents * (1 + TAX_RATE))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef final_total(subtotal_cents: int, code: str | None = None) -> int:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Total the customer pays for a given subtotal and optional discount code.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    # Discount is applied before tax, per store policy.\\\\n    taxed = apply_tax(subtotal_cents)\\\\n    return apply_discount(taxed, code)\\\\n\\\"}\",\"id\":\"call_741822\"},{\"type\":\"tool_call_response\",\"response\":\"{\\\"output\\\":\\\"import pytest\\\\n\\\\nfrom shopcart import Cart\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_empty_cart_total_is_zero():\\\\n    assert Cart().total() == 0\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_add_single_item():\\\\n    cart = Cart()\\\\n    cart.add_item(\\\\\\\"MUG\\\\\\\")\\\\n    assert cart.items == {\\\\\\\"MUG\\\\\\\": 1}\\\\n    assert cart.subtotal() == 1200\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_add_same_item_twice_increments_quantity():\\\\n    cart = Cart()\\\\n    cart.add_item(\\\\\\\"MUG\\\\\\\")\\\\n    cart.add_item(\\\\\\\"MUG\\\\\\\", 2)\\\\n    assert cart.items == {\\\\\\\"MUG\\\\\\\": 3}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_remove_item_decrements_then_deletes():\\\\n    cart = Cart()\\\\n    cart.add_item(\\\\\\\"CAP\\\\\\\", 2)\\\\n    cart.remove_item(\\\\\\\"CAP\\\\\\\")\\\\n    assert cart.items == {\\\\\\\"CAP\\\\\\\": 1}\\\\n    cart.remove_item(\\\\\\\"CAP\\\\\\\")\\\\n    assert cart.items == {}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_unknown_sku_raises():\\\\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\\\\n        Cart().add_item(\\\\\\\"NOPE\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_invalid_code_raises():\\\\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\\\\n        Cart().apply_code(\\\\\\\"FREESTUFF\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_total_includes_tax():\\\\n    cart = Cart()\\\\n    cart.add_item(\\\\\\\"TEE\\\\\\\")\\\\n    assert cart.total() == 2160  # 2000 + 8% tax\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_percent_discount():\\\\n    cart = Cart()\\\\n    cart.add_item(\\\\\\\"MUG\\\\\\\", 2)\\\\n    cart.apply_code(\\\\\\\"SAVE10\\\\\\\")\\\\n    assert cart.total() == 2333  # (2400 - 10%) + 8% tax\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_fixed_discount_applied_before_tax():\\\\n    cart = Cart()\\\\n    cart.add_item(\\\\\\\"TEE\\\\\\\")\\\\n    cart.add_item(\\\\\\\"TEE\\\\\\\")\\\\n    cart.apply_code(\\\\\\\"TENOFF\\\\\\\")\\\\n    assert cart.total() == 3240  # (4000 - 1000) + 8% tax\\\\n\\\"}\",\"id\":\"call_741825\"},{\"type\":\"tool_call_response\",\"response\":\"{\\\"output\\\":\\\"import pytest\\\\n\\\\nfrom shopcart.pricing import apply_discount, apply_tax\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_apply_tax():\\\\n    assert apply_tax(1000) == 1080\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_no_code_means_no_discount():\\\\n    assert apply_discount(1000, None) == 1000\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_percent_discount():\\\\n    assert apply_discount(2000, \\\\\\\"SAVE25\\\\\\\") == 1500\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_fixed_discount_never_negative():\\\\n    assert apply_discount(500, \\\\\\\"TENOFF\\\\\\\") == 0\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef test_invalid_code_raises():\\\\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\\\\n        apply_discount(1000, \\\\\\\"BOGUS\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\"}\",\"id\":\"call_741828\"}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"parts\":[{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"name\":\"run_shell_command\",\"id\":\"call_1695\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m pytest\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Run pytest to check failing tests\\\"}\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"type\":\"tool_call_response\",\"response\":\"{\\\"output\\\":\\\"<untrusted_context>\\\\nOutput: ===================================================== test session starts ======================================================\\\\nplatform linux -- Python 3.12.3, pytest-9.2.0, pluggy-1.7.0\\\\nrootdir: /home/simra/cse115a/lab/AI-Augmented-Software-Engineering/assignments/03-anatomy-of-coding-agents/gemini-cli-dissection/work/run\\\\ncollected 14 items                                                                                                             \\\\n\\\\ntests/test_cart.py ..F.....F                                                                                             [ 64%]\\\\ntests/test_pricing.py .....                                                                                              [100%]\\\\n\\\\n=========================================================== FAILURES ===========================================================\\\\n_________________________________________ test_add_same_item_twice_increments_quantity _________________________________________\\\\n\\\\n    def test_add_same_item_twice_increments_quantity():\\\\n        cart = Cart()\\\\n        cart.add_item(\\\\\\\"MUG\\\\\\\")\\\\n        cart.add_item(\\\\\\\"MUG\\\\\\\", 2)\\\\n>       assert cart.items == {\\\\\\\"MUG\\\\\\\": 3}\\\\nE       AssertionError: assert {'MUG': 2} == {'MUG': 3}\\\\nE         \\\\nE         Differing items:\\\\nE         {'MUG': 2} != {'MUG': 3}\\\\nE         Use -v to get more diff\\\\n\\\\ntests/test_cart.py:21: AssertionError\\\\n____________________________________________ test_fixed_discount_applied_before_tax ____________________________________________\\\\n\\\\n    def test_fixed_discount_applied_before_tax():\\\\n        cart = Cart()\\\\n        cart.add_item(\\\\\\\"TEE\\\\\\\")\\\\n        cart.add_item(\\\\\\\"TEE\\\\\\\")\\\\n        cart.apply_code(\\\\\\\"TENOFF\\\\\\\")\\\\n>       assert cart.total() == 3240  # (4000 - 1000) + 8% tax\\\\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\\\nE       assert 1160 == 3240\\\\nE        +  where 1160 = total()\\\\nE        +    where total = <shopcart.cart.Cart object at 0x7a0709466480>.total\\\\n\\\\ntests/test_cart.py:61: AssertionError\\\\n=================================================== short test summary info ====================================================\\\\nFAILED tests/test_cart.py::test_add_same_item_twice_increments_quantity - AssertionError: assert {'MUG': 2} == {'MUG': 3}\\\\nFAILED tests/test_cart.py::test_fixed_discount_applied_before_tax - assert 1160 == 3240\\\\n================================================= 2 failed, 12 passed in 0.05s =================================================\\\\nExit Code: 1\\\\nProcess Group PGID: 15314\\\\n</untrusted_context>\\\"}\",\"id\":\"call_1695\"}]}]",
